@v721 kernel.seq.make item "animal classification" item "plant classification" item "solar system" item "water states" item "plane shapes" item "duration and measurement" item "everyday object categories" item "countries and capitals" item "named calendar cycles" item "verbal arithmetic" item "family and other named relations" item "qualitative ordering" item "spatial containment"
@v722 kernel.seq.make item "A finite introductory vocabulary, not a complete school curriculum." item "Rules describe explicit taxonomic categories, not default abilities or living status. No universal bird-flight or mammal-live-birth rule is supplied." item "General conversation, pronouns, flexible paraphrases, temporal change and unrestricted why/how explanations are not learned by these data." item "Unit counts are declared exact duration facts, not a general unit-conversion solver." item "What-is answers select supported category names. They are not free-form generated definitions." item "Category definitions and instance classification share an explicit kind relation. The vocabulary separates category constants from ordinary named examples by teaching convention, not a general higher-order type system." item "Source citations support the authored claims; the formal proof checker verifies entailment and spans, not external source truth." item "The optional initializer is explicit and must be used through a model-bound session snapshot until a shared fact-fragments bootstrap linkage is installed." item "Geography includes two countries and their capitals. It does not claim worldwide coverage or political-border reasoning." item "Calendar questions use adjacent successors and predecessors in named cycles. They do not establish general temporal reasoning." item "Biological flight claims include the penguin exclusion, without assuming that every member of a flying bird species can fly." item "The source-supervised revision was developed after the imported compatibility cases were visible. Its rules and language are authored, not induced from an independent curriculum."
